<DocsLayout
  title="Documentation that follows the code."
  description="StateKnot documentation distinguishes implemented evidence from active design work and planned v1 capabilities."
  section="Overview"
>
  <aside class="docs-callout" aria-labelledby="docs-boundary-title">
    <h2 id="docs-boundary-title">The honest starting point</h2>
    <p>
      StateKnot does not yet expose a stable public model/tool Agent API. Today
      you can compile a deterministic Graph, freeze its executable deployment,
      replay noninitial checkpoints, and run a tenant-scoped durable Graph loop
      through atomic lifecycle commits on PostgreSQL. Provider-neutral durable
      model/tool attempts, weighted cross-tenant selection, a typed Agent
      contract, and the first OpenAI Responses and Anthropic Messages adapters
      are also implemented. Atomic durable Agent admission binds those contracts
      to scheduler-visible work, while durable ingress keys and the public
      run/result facade recover lost acknowledgements and verify terminal reads.
      The <a href="/docs/provider-native-agent/"
        >prebuilt provider-native Agent graph</a
      > now adds recovered multi-turn Tools, policy, accounting, and exact cancellation.
      <a href="/docs/agent-service/">AgentService v1</a> now exposes submission, verified
      reads, and cancellation as an authorization-first embedding boundary. The <a
        href="/docs/mcp-client/">general MCP Tool client</a
      > now adds bounded dynamic discovery, JSON/request-scoped SSE, custom headers,
      MRTR, and <a href="/docs/mcp-oauth/">interactive OAuth authorization</a>;
      the <a href="/docs/mcp-remote-tool/">strict MCP Remote Tool profile</a> preserves
      the stronger durable binding. The <a href="/docs/mcp-server/"
        >MCP Server profile</a
      > now exposes bounded Tools, Resources, Prompts, Completion, and MRTR behind
      the strict production transport. The <a href="/docs/a2a-server/"
        >A2A 1.0 Server profile</a
      > now adds bounded Agent Card, messaging, task, streaming, cancellation, resubscription,
      and push-management boundaries across HTTP+JSON, JSON-RPC, and SSE; its <a
        href="/docs/a2a-conformance/">frozen official TCK gate</a
      >
      passes 177 cases with zero failures or errors. Stable network Agent transport,
      MCP Tasks, a production durable A2A task/push backend, the A2A Client, gRPC,
      and production qualification remain release blockers.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <section aria-labelledby="choose-path-title">
