          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="docs-surface-title">
    <h2 id="docs-surface-title">What these docs cover now</h2>
    <dl class="docs-definition-list">
      <div>
        <dt>Core contracts</dt>
        <dd>
          Typed, bounded domain values for agents, models, tools, runs, compiled
          graphs, deterministic barriers, checkpoints, invocations, waits,
          results, and recovery evidence.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>PostgreSQL durability</dt>
        <dd>
          Exact migrations, journal and checkpoint integrity, leases and
          fencing, invocation ledgers, pending results, barriers, durable waits,
          outbox delivery, quarantine, ready-node recovery planning, indexed
          delayed-retry wakeups, and the tenant-scoped immutable graph registry.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Durable Graph runtime</dt>
        <dd>
          Offline executable registration, independent bounded replay,
          durable-before-dispatch node execution, lease renewal, automatic
          Continue barriers, and typed lifecycle handoffs.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Lifecycle and Agent Loop</dt>
        <dd>
          Trusted terminal evidence, database-time Wait registration, atomic
          success/failure transitions, exact lost-ack convergence, bounded
          cleanup, and one tenant-scoped scheduler quantum.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Atomic Agent admission</dt>
        <dd>
          Authenticated immutable intent, deterministic finite budgets,
          database-clock commit, sequence-one audit event, superstep-zero
          checkpoint, exact lost-ack retry, and fully verified durable loads.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Durable Agent runs and results</dt>
        <dd>
          Tenant-scoped ingress idempotency, fresh-ID retry convergence,
          verified public lifecycle snapshots, terminal results, and fail-closed
          run/key lookups.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>AgentService v1</dt>
        <dd>
          Exact-version deployment binding, authorization before existence
          disclosure, durable submission recovery, verified reads, and
          caller-retained two-phase cancellation identities.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Typed Agent and provider adapters</dt>
        <dd>
          Generated, canonical digest-pinned input/output schemas; offline
          provider-profile binding; bounded typed request/result validation; and
          first-party OpenAI Responses and Anthropic Messages unary and SSE
          transports.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>General MCP Tool client</dt>
        <dd>
          Bounded stateless discovery and pagination, JSON/request-scoped SSE,
          standard and nested custom headers, invalid-Tool isolation,
          request-scoped authorization, no network schema dereference, and exact
          multi-round request state.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Strict MCP Remote Tool</dt>
        <dd>
          MCP 2026-07-28 modern discovery, stateless complete-JSON transport,
          exact local schema and server-identity pins, attempt-scoped
          authorization, and reconciliation-first lost-write behavior.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Architecture decisions</dt>
        <dd>
          Draft RFCs and qualification scenarios that constrain implementation;
          drafts are not stable compatibility promises.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="api-reference-title">
